miumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/92/1524792/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9e1943311a8a9f9427cc0cff6e2762c966a7ad84" commit="eb30ab23a072805dd3d4a81c6e8f31ce02aa5b54" commit_message="Add a SPI command class to `struct flashchip`  This is a backport of `commit 31b5e3bf` upstream;  By default, we want to probe for SPI25 chips only. Other SPI use cases, like the ENE/EDI protocol, might use commands that can confuse these common chips.  Now, flashrom will probe for a chip only if one of these conditions is true: 1) no chip has been specified AND the chip uses the SPI25 commands 2) this chip has been specified by -c | --chip &lt;chipname&gt;  The CLI can later be extended to probe for a specific class of chips.  Signed-off-by: Mike Banon &lt;mikebdp2@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Nico Huber &lt;nico.h@gmx.de&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/23262 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) &lt;no-reply@coreboot.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Kocialkowski &lt;contact@paulk.fr&gt;  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=still builds  Change-Id: I9e1943311a8a9f9427cc0cff6e2762c966a7ad84 Signed-off-by: Edward O'Callaghan &lt;quasisec@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1484920 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="1484920" owner_email="quasisec@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/20/1484920/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8f7b5899a8ea2c75174de46e95d935d1bf4ab934" commit="2aa896aba00a324877eee66bd9c3b8e702b39d22" commit_message="Refine granularity handling in preparation of AT45DB serie